Get-Service

Displays all Windows services and their current status.

Useful for: 
Checking whether services are running or stopped  
Diagnosing system or application issues  Managing services via scripts

Detailed Explanation A service runs in the background without user interaction Many Windows features depend on services

Get-Service | Where-Object Status -eq Running



-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Start-Service

Starts a stopped Windows service.

Useful for: Starting required services after troubleshooting  Automating service startup in scripts  Recovering services that stopped unexpectedly

Detailed Explanation Windows services run in the background  Some applications depend on services to function  This command avoids opening Services.msc manually

Start-Service -Name <ServiceName>

Start-Service -Name Spooler

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Stop-Service

Stops a running Windows service.

Stop-Service -Name <ServiceName>

Stop-Service -Name Spooler

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Restart-Service

Stops and then starts a service in one command.

Detailed Explanation Combines Stop-Service and Start-Service

Restart-Service -Name <ServiceName>

Restart-Service -Name Spooler

